    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0642" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660M116/3a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Lithuania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d455-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-06T17:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Please submit as soon as possible by mail comprehensive report on the present
                    treatment by Lithuania of American trade. Legation at Riga has been requested to
                    forward you a copy of a report from Tallinn<anchor n="3" xml:id="d455-f2"/> to
                    serve in form and content as a model. Special efforts should be made to obtain
                    comparable information from Lithuanian officials and importers. Your report
                    should show definitely whether American trade is at the present time receiving
                    most-favored-nation treatment in Lithuania and, if not, precisely wherein such
                    treatment is being denied.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d455-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d455-f1-content">
                <p>The Minister was accredited to Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania, with residence at
                    Riga.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d455-f2" n="3" xml:id="d455-f2-content">
                <p>Despatch No. 43, October 6, 1934, <ref target="frus1934v02#pg_130"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1934, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 130</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
